  "scope": "Complete general coarea for Lipschitz f:R^m to R^n, m>n, every Lebesgue-measurable source A, infinite integral values and n=0. Both actual integral graphs have the same value; no Borel, finite-mass, rank, differentiability or slicing hypothesis is added. Prove full rank by 3.2.9/3.2.10 and the critical case by the exact perturbation, adjoint Jacobian bound, fibre isometry, completed joint measurability, Fubini, closed-ball volume and epsilon removal. Apply erratum p.5, book p.249 line21: source factor L^m(A).",
